1
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Just because you're invited, doesn't mean you're welcome.

2
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Get Out is a mystery, thriller, horror film directed by Jordan Peele.

3
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Chris and his girlfriend Rose go upstate to visit her parents for the weekend.

4
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
At first, Chris reads the family's overly accommodating behavior as nervous attempts to deal with their daughter's interracial relationship, but
as the weekend progresses, a series of increasingly disturbing discoveries lead him to a truth that he never could have imagined.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Chris Washington, played by Daniel Kaluuya.

6
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Rose Armitage, played by Allison Williams.

7
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Missy Armitage, played by Catherine Keener.

8
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Dean Armitage, played by Bradley Whitford.

9
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Jeremy Armitage, played by Caleb Landry Jones.

10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Walter, played by Marcus Henderson.

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Get Out is a 2017 American psychological horror film written,
co-produced, and directed by Jordan Peele in his directorial debut.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
It stars Daniel Kaluuya, Allison Williams, Lil Rel Howery, LaKeith Stanfield, Bradley
Whitford, Caleb Landry Jones, Stephen Root, Catherine Keener, and Betty Gabriel.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
The plot follows a young black man (Kaluuya), who uncovers shocking secrets
when he meets the family of his white girlfriend (Williams).

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Principal photography began in February 2016 in Fairhope, Alabama, then moved to
Barton Academy and the Ashland Place Historic District in Mobile, Alabama.

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The entire film was shot in 23 days.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
It premiered at the Sundance Film Festival on January 23, 2017, and was theatrically
released in the United States on February 24, 2017, by Universal Pictures.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
The film received critical acclaim for its screenplay,
direction, acting, and social critiques.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It was a major commercial success, grossing $255 million worldwide on a $4.5 million budget, with
a net profit of $124.3 million, making it the tenth-most profitable film of 2017.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
It was chosen by the National Board of Review, the American Film
Institute, and Time as one of the top ten films of the year.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
It won many accolades, including the Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay for Peele at the 90th Academy
Awards, with additional nominations for Best Picture, Best Director and Best Actor (Kaluuya).

21
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
It also earned five nominations at the 23rd Critics' Choice Awards, two at the 75th Golden Globe
Awards, the 71st British Academy Film Awards and the 24th Screen Actors Guild Awards.

22
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:26,000
The film explores themes of kidnapping, externally controlled
action, manipulation, dark comedy, hypnosis.

23
01:39:40,000 --> 01:39:46,000
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
